</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> covers DPO (Direct Preference Optimisation), while Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> presents the Robust DPO formulation, which introduces noise to simulate flipped preferences and incorporates a conservative loss function. Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Proof of Lemma ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> provides the Proof of Lemma 1, detailing the theoretical underpinnings supporting the main results. Finally, Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Noisy 2D-DPO Algorithm ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> describes the Noisy 2D-DPO Algorithm, which extends the DPO approach by incorporating two-dimensional noise to enhance robustness and optimize performance in more complex scenarios. Finally, Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Experiment 5 results ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> elaborates on the set-up and results of Experiment 5 as mentioned in Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rafailov et. al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> proposed DPO where the reward model was written in terms of the policy as shown in Eq. <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{r^{\ast}}(s,{a})\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}(a|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}(a|s)}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log{Z^{\ast}}(s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{r^{\ast}}(s,{a})\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}(a|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}(a|s)}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log{Z^{\ast}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{Z^{\ast}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{Z^{\ast}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">partition function</span>. Substituting from Eq. <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> to the standard BTL model as proposed by Bradley et. al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, we get the preference probabilities as seen in Eq. <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left[\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}({a_{w}}|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}({a_{w}}|s)}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt-\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}({a_{l}}|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}({a_{l}}|s)}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left[\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}({a_{w}}|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}({a_{w}}|s)}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt-\hskip 2.84544pt\beta\log\left(\frac{{\pi^{\ast}}({a_{l}}|s)}{{\pi^{\text{SFT}}}({a_{l}}|s)}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can define the margin of difference between the reward scores for preferred and rejected responses as shown in Eq. <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt{r_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}})-{r_{\theta}}(s,{a_{l}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt{r_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}})-{r_{\theta}}(s,{a_{l}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back in Eq. <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Proof for Direct Preference Optimisation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, we get -</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left[\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left[\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This will enable us to formulate the loss that we wish to minimize -</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 1.42271pt;\hskip 1.42271pts,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt-\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.140em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 1.42271pt;\hskip 1.42271pts,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt-\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Robust DPO formulation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given corrupted dataset <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can use Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Problem Setup and Background ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to get the expression in Eq. <a href="#A2.E23" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt-\log{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt-\log{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We know that the preferences are flipped with a small probability of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can write the predicted probabilities under noisy preferences as shown in Eq. <a href="#A2.E24" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right){\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon{\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{l}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{w}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\\
&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.727em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.727em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.727em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right){\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon{\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{l}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{w}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\\
&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We know that the logarithmic function is concave, we can write the following expression -</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\log{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left\{\left(1-\epsilon\right)\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\right\}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;\geq\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.727em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\log{\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{\tilde{a}_{w}}\succ{\tilde{a}_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left\{\left(1-\epsilon\right)\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\right\}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;\geq\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The result from Eq. <a href="#A2.E25" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> can be used to upper bound the loss since the loss is nothing but the negative of the LHS of Eq. <a href="#A2.E25" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>. In other words, we can have the noisy loss as -</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\\
&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right){\mathcal{L}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)+\epsilon{\mathcal{L}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right)\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt+\hskip 2.84544pt\epsilon\hskip 1.42271pt\log\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\right)\\
&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\left(1-\epsilon\right){\mathcal{L}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)+\epsilon{\mathcal{L}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{l}},{\tilde{a}_{w}}\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The loss in Eq. <a href="#A2.E26" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> is called the <span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conservative DPO</span> loss. However, there is a problem with this formulation. We have -</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{{a}_{w}},{{a}_{l}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≠</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{{a}_{w}},{{a}_{l}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{{a}_{w}},{{a}_{l}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≠</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{\tilde{a}_{w}},{\tilde{a}_{l}}\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{L}\left(\theta\hskip 2.84544pt;\hskip 2.84544pts,{{a}_{w}},{{a}_{l}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≠</mo><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)\hskip 2.84544pt\neq\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The above equations point to the fact that the loss formulation is biased and there is a need to find an unbiased version of this loss formulation. Chowdhury et. al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> further propose an unbiased preference probability expression as shown in Eq. <a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{l}},{a_{w}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{l}},{a_{w}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Using the definition of the Logit function, we can see that -</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{logit}\left({\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{logit}\left({\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left({\mathbb{P}_{\theta}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Sanity Check for Eq. <a href="#A2.E28" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We know from Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Problem Setup and Background ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> -</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us consider the log-odds of the sigmoid function.</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathrm{logit}\left(\sigma(x)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\sigma(x)}{1-\sigma(x)}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\sigma(x)}{\sigma(-x)}\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}}{\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1}\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544ptx\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.560em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mfrac><mo rspace="0.560em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathrm{logit}\left(\sigma(x)\right)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\sigma(x)}{1-\sigma(x)}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\sigma(x)}{\sigma(-x)}\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}}{\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1}\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544ptx\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the result in Eq. <a href="#A2.E30" title="In B.1 Sanity Check for Eq. ‣ Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> in Eq. <a href="#A2.E29" title="In B.1 Sanity Check for Eq. ‣ Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, we get -</p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathrm{logit}\left[\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left[\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\right)\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>logit</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathrm{logit}\left[\mathbb{P}\left({a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right)\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{logit}\left[\sigma\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\right)\right]\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let us assume that</p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})=z\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{(say)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>say</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{h_{\theta}}(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}})=z\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{(say)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Then, Eq. <a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> becomes -</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}{\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{l}},{a_{w}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(-\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{{\sigma(-z)}^{\epsilon}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544ptA\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{(say)}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" rspace="0.727em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.838em" rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.560em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>say</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}{\hat{\mathbb{P}}_{\theta,\epsilon}}\left[{a_{w}}\succ{a_{l}}\hskip 2.84544pt|\hskip 2.84544pts\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{l}},{a_{w}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\sigma{{\left(\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}}{\sigma{{\left(-\beta{h_{\theta}}\left(s,{a_{w}},{a_{l}}\right)\right)}^{\epsilon}}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{{\sigma(-z)}^{\epsilon}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}\\
\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544ptA\hskip 2.84544pt\mathrm{(say)}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">After defining <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A2.E33" title="In B.1 Sanity Check for Eq. ‣ Appendix B Robust DPO formulation ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>, we can write -</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{A}{1-A}\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}}{1-\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{A}{1-A}\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}}{1-\frac{{\sigma(z)}^{(1-\epsilon)}}{\left[{1-\sigma(z)}\right]^{\epsilon}}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">This shall motivate the formulation of an unbiased loss function that has been written in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem Setup and Background ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ 4.2 High-Level Noise-Robust 2D-DPO Formulation ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a value <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and the standard sigmoid function -</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(-x)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(-x)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">To prove necessity</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">We need to show that -</p>
<table id="A3.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))\hskip 8.5359pt\implies\hskip 8.5359ptx=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.850em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))\hskip 8.5359pt\implies\hskip 8.5359ptx=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding the sigmoid in Eq. <a href="#A3.E35" title="In Appendix C Proof of Lemma ‣ Inducing Robustness in a 2-dimensional Direct Preference Optimisation Paradigm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>, we get -</p>
<table id="A3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\exp{(-x)}}{1+\exp{(-x)}}\right]\\
\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{\exp{(-x)}}{1+\exp{(-x)}}\right]\\
\log\left[\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\log\left[\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}\right]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the monotonicity property of the <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math>, we get -</p>
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}\\
\exp(x)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt1\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.838em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\exp{(x)}}{1+\exp{(x)}}\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(x)}}\\
\exp(x)\hskip 2.84544pt&amp;=\hskip 2.84544pt1\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the only possible value <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> can take is <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">To prove sufficiency</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">We need to show that -</p>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0\hskip 8.5359pt\implies\hskip 8.5359pt\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="1.128em" rspace="1.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0\hskip 8.5359pt\implies\hskip 8.5359pt\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the sigmpoid function, we get -</p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x=0)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\exp{(0)}}{1+\exp{(0)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x=0)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{\exp{(0)}}{1+\exp{(0)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we have -</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x=-0)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(0)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x=-0)\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{1+\exp{(0)}}\hskip 2.84544pt=\hskip 2.84544pt\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we can say that if <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we get <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\sigma(x))=\log(\sigma(-x))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Noisy 2D-DPO Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Noisy 2D-DPO Optimisation via Mini Batch GD</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input : </span> Parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, Policy model <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reference policy <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Temperature <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, Learning rate <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, Mini-batch size <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, Number of training iterations <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>  iteration from <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            Initialize: Mini batch <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\left\{{\tau_{w}^{(i)}},{\tau_{l}^{(i)}},{r_{w}^{(i)}},{r_{l}^{(i)}}\right\}_{i=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\left\{{\tau_{w}^{(i)}},{\tau_{l}^{(i)}},{r_{w}^{(i)}},{r_{l}^{(i)}}\right\}_{i=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, Gradient Accumulator <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{g_{\mathrm{batch}}}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>batch</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{g_{\mathrm{batch}}}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>  <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
             Sample Noise <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sim U(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sim U(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, Initialize Sample Loss <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{L_{\mathrm{sample}}}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>sample</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{L_{\mathrm{sample}}}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>  <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{n^{(i)}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{n^{(i)}}-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
